WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.720
This is London's Cable Car, the £60 million boondoggle

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.060
that the Mayor of London insisted was
a vital part of the city's transport infrastructure.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:17.020
And here's the thing.
That is a really tall cable car, 90 metres.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.440
If you want a cable car with a view over the city,

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.360
you don't need it to be that high.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.500
Why is it so tall?
Well, the answer to that is down the river,

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.620
at the QE2 Bridge, at the Dartford Crossing, which for many years has been the height limit

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:34.680
for vessels, cruise ships, warships coming into the city.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.340
Now, when this cable car was built, one of the requirements was that those ships could not be impeded.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.100
They must still be able to come into London.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:45.080
But here's something you might not know.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:50.260
This height, this expensive height here, is a compromise. Every metre you ratchet up the height,

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:55.720
you also ratchet up the cost, but it has to be
high enough to let those vessels pass underneath.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:59.780
And the thing you might not know is that, well, the way they bodged it

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:03.160
is that if a tall ship needs to
come underneath at low tide,

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.160
they will remove all the gondolas

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:08.340
and make sure there's no passengers on board. Put everything safely away.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:14.220
So that the wire, unladen, raises up enough to let boats pass.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.660
It is a bodge job at best.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:20.980
but then that pretty much sums up
the Mayor of London.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.480
And that is something you might not know.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:28.040
